      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xpuf__client__api_1ga03926d586e353bb459b3da51ae7e4e8b" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int XPuf_GetServerLibInfo</definition>
        <argsstring>(XPuf_ClientInstance *InstancePtr, Xil_LibInfo *LibInfo)</argsstring>
        <name>XPuf_GetServerLibInfo</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_puf___client_instance" kindref="compound">XPuf_ClientInstance</ref> *</type>
          <declname>InstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>Xil_LibInfo *</type>
          <declname>LibInfo</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sends an IPI request to get the XilPuf library version and capability bits running on the PLM. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the client instance </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>LibInfo</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to Xil_LibInfo. LibVersion and Capability are filled on success. The Version and NistStatus fields are reserved for XilPuf and must be ignored.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS if the library information is read successfully</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM if any input parameter is invalid</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE if there is a failure </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Perform input parameter validation. Return XST_INVALID_PARAM if input parameters are invalid.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Query library info via the Features command using a valid PUF api-id as the selector, so the command succeeds and the server returns the library version/capability at fixed indices.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Send request to server via SMC for EL1 non-secure AArch64 applications or via IPI mailbox for other environments.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>        </inbodydescription>
